ass_rate":0.5857,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6471,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1587},{"week":17,"opponent":"NYG","home":false,"pf":34.0,"pa":17.0,"off_snaps":72,"epa_per_play":0.06749,"pass_rate":0.5694,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5968,"def_epa_per_play":-0.2487}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"CLE","distance":0.5562,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"},{"season":2023,"team":"NE","distance":0.5586,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.7664,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DEN","distance":0.7701,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2018,"team":"HOU","distance":0.8226,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2019,"team":"CIN","distance":0.6151,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2025,"team":"CLE","distance":0.658,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.7144,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"CAR","distance":0.7568,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"CIN","distance":0.7931,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Eagles went 9-7 in 2019 and outscored opponents 385 to 354. The offense ranked 18th in EPA per play and the defense 13th in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. Their most distinctive traits were the highest 12 personnel usage and the 3rd highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Eagles offense was about average by EPA per play. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the highest 12 personnel usage and the 2nd most tight ends on the field in the league. Carson Wentz ran the passing game, with Zach Ertz leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Eagles defense was a little above average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 4th and 17th. Fletcher Cox was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Vinny Curry, who had 5 sacks while playing only 40% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they had the 3rd highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Eagles were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 85% of field goals, which was a little above average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their linebackers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Carson Wentz played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,039 yards. Zach Ertz was the clear top target with 22% of the looks and 916 receiving yards. The backfield was a committee led by Miles Sanders and Jordan Howard. On defense, Brandon Graham led the team with 8.5 sacks and Rodney McLeod picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Browns under Kevin Stefanski and the 2023 Patriots. Their defense looked most like the 2019 Bengals under Lou Anarumo and the 2025 Browns.","trends":"The offense went from 13th in EPA per play in 2018 to 18th in 2019, a modest decline. The defense moved from 19th in EPA allowed per play in 2018 to 13th in 2019, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was number of defenders in the box, which went from 6.34 to 6.65.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2019. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}